Why should testing data be kept separate? 

Your AI model may simply learn about the specific attacks but not how to identify them and counterattack them.  

 

 

What could be a false positive? 

The admin is getting locked out of the system. This can happen if the model performs a routine maintenance task and incorrectly identifies the admin as a threat.  

What could be a false negative? 

If malware enters the network and the model identifies it as normal, giving the Attacker access to important data.  

Would precision or recall be more important? 

In cybersecurity, Recall is more important. A false negative can lead to the loss of very important data while false positives are annoying and create extra work for the person operating all these systems. So, we prioritize finding catching many attacks, even if it means sometimes wasting time and resources one false alarm.  

